    {
      "id": 5596,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-10T23:35:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Not the infinite loop combo alluded to in other questions but a pretty devastating one all the same.</p>\n<p>As I understand it (and I’m perfectly happy to be proved very wrong) the Demoralization/Darken the Sky combo doesn’t work because Demoralization isn’t a triggered effect, it is evaluated at the end of each action.<br>\nHairtrigger Reflexes has a trigger and is thus constantly evaluated, twigging off as soon as the trigger condition is met (a villain card entering play).<br>\nDarken the Sky doesn’t pull all fowl cards out of the trash first and then play then one at a time from the villains (temporary, entirely fictional) ‘hand’, it pulls and plays the fowls cards one at a time until the trash is empty of fowl cards.</p>\n<p>So if Darken the Sky is played with Hairtrigger Reflexes in play does this kill all the heroes? (or, more accurately, everyone who has less HP than Expatriette, and herself)</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:17.622Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 5,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 25.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 5594,
      "topic_slug": "hairtrigger-reflexes-and-darken-the-sky",
      "display_username": "Matchstickman",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
